        "description": "Requires a workspace API token; Zapier OAuth credentials are rejected. Creates another audience link on the room, in any access mode, and the per-document tracked shares it needs. Supply at least one recipient or company field. Names and emails find or create a contact; companyName finds or creates a company; supplying both associates the contact with the company. Existing contactId/companyId values must belong to the authenticated workspace. A refused call (a plan gate, a missing room, an archived room) leaves no link, company, or contact behind.\n\nOptions the workspace's plan does not include return 403 FEATURE_NOT_AVAILABLE rather than being dropped. A verified-allowlist link needs at least one of allowedEmails or allowedDomains.\n\nWorkspace API keys need both `rooms:write` and `crm:write`; every valid request resolves recipient or company fields against CRM records.",
